# Classified observer-parity findings, as of 2026-07-29.
#
# Every line without a leading `#` is a hit that has been triaged. The comments
# ARE the audit: a hit with no rationale above it has not been classified, and
# the audit has not passed. See docs/plans/observer-parity-audits.md for what
# each check is looking for and docs/plans/observer-parity-harness.md for the
# boundaries they sit on.
#
# Lines beginning `# OPEN:` are reprinted by the script on every run. Use them
# for hits that are correctly classified and still wrong — a green exit means
# "nothing new", never "nothing wrong".
#
# Regenerate with `./observer-parity.sh --update` (comments are preserved).
#
# --- A1 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: 43 entity-keyed `find(...)` sites, every one triaged by recovery
# mechanism in the audits doc (spawn packet, lazy re-request, or transient).
# This is a tripwire on the COUNT: a new site is a new handler to classify.
# Re-run whenever a NetworkEvent is added.
#
# 40 -> 43 on 2026-07-29, from the three phase-1 handlers. All three recover
# via the spawn packet, so a miss is harmless:
#   ChangeLook      — every look type it carries rides EntityData
#   EntityDirection — `direction` comes from entity_data.position
#   EntityStopMove  — position/movement are rebuilt from EntityData
# That is the distinction that matters: ammunition needed an off-entity map
# because it has NO spawn-packet slot. None of these three do.
A1|entity-keyed-find-sites=43
#
# --- A2 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: all eight are re-derived at construction from EntityData, so an
# `AddEntity` rebuild cannot lose them:
#   position/tile_position/world_position/direction  <- entity_data.position
#   active_movement                                  <- entity_data.destination
#   entity_type, scale                               <- job_id at construction
#   animation_data, in_safe_zone                     <- set explicitly after
# A field appearing here that is NOT in that list is a rebuild-wipe bug.
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=active_movement
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=animation_data
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=direction
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=entity_type
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=in_safe_zone
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=scale
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=tile_position
A2|common-field-not-in-entitydata=world_position
#
# --- A3 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: no hits. Clean since the hair fix (2026-07-29) moved `head` onto
# `Common`. Any hit here is appearance state invisible to every observer,
# because remote players are built as `Entity::Npc`. Run this audit BEFORE
# shipping headgear, robe or dye, which will otherwise land in the same trap.
#
# --- A9 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mutations one path performs and the other does not. Valid classifications
# are "derived from EntityData at construction" or "transient". Anything else
# is drift between two pieces of code nothing keeps in step.
#
# why (derived in `Common::new` / `Npc::new`, so a rebuild reproduces them):
#   set_position   <- entity_data.position          (entity/mod.rs:1115-1117)
#   move_from_to   <- entity_data.destination       (entity/mod.rs:2099-2107)
#   set_weapon     <- entity_data.weapon            (entity/mod.rs:1093)
#   set_shield     <- entity_data.shield            (entity/mod.rs:1094)
#   set_sit/revive <- entity_data.state 1=dead 2=sit(entity/mod.rs:1101-1103)
#   set_idle       <- same match, default arm
#   set_look       <- all seven look slots are seeded from EntityData in
#                     `Common::new` (entity/mod.rs), which is the whole reason
#                     ChangeLook needs no off-entity map. Added 2026-07-29.
# why (transient): clear_cast — `active_cast: None` at construction
#   (entity/mod.rs:1142). A rebuild does drop an in-flight cast bar, which
#   matches the server: enter-view has no cast re-send either (harness §3.5).
# why (deliberately AddEntity-only): inherit_fade_state — the one thing a
#   replacement entity is meant to carry over. See A2.
A9|addentity-only-mutator=inherit_fade_state
A9|local-only-mutator=clear_cast
A9|local-only-mutator=move_from_to
A9|local-only-mutator=revive
A9|local-only-mutator=set_idle
A9|local-only-mutator=set_look
A9|local-only-mutator=set_position
A9|local-only-mutator=set_shield
A9|local-only-mutator=set_sit
A9|local-only-mutator=set_weapon
#
# OPEN: A9 — refresh_neutral_stance is called on the local player
# OPEN:      (lib.rs:7226, right after set_in_safe_zone) and NEVER on the
# OPEN:      AddEntity path (lib.rs:3691 sets the safe zone and stops). It is
# OPEN:      not derived either: `Common::new` picks the stance at
# OPEN:      entity/mod.rs:1106 with `idle(entity_type, true, ...)` — ready
# OPEN:      fight hardcoded, no safe-zone term — while in_safe_zone is still
# OPEN:      its `false` default (1132), and set_in_safe_zone runs afterwards
# OPEN:      without restancing. It does not self-heal: return_to_neutral
# OPEN:      (animation/mod.rs:602) forces ReadyFight whenever previous_state
# OPEN:      is 2|4|8, and ReadyFight is 4.
# OPEN:      Predicted symptom: an armed remote player who spawns into view on
# OPEN:      a town map stands battle-ready to that observer until they walk.
# OPEN:      The local player was fixed for this in abb519f1; the remote path
# OPEN:      never was. CODE-READ ONLY — confirm on two clients before fixing.
A9|local-only-mutator=refresh_neutral_stance
#
# --- A4 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: latent, not live. All three are broadcast before `map->addblock` in
# `clif_parse_LoadEndAck`, so the AREA send reaches nobody — but the spawn
# packet re-supplies weapon and shield to every arriving observer, so the
# value is right anyway. Becomes a real bug the instant a look type NOT
# carried by the spawn packet is added here. That is exactly how the
# LOOK_AMMO login seed failed. Wants a comment at the site, not a fix.
A4|before-addblock=clif->changelook(&sd->bl, LOOK_SHIELD, sd->status.look.shield);
A4|before-addblock=clif->changelook(&sd->bl, LOOK_WEAPON, 0);
A4|before-addblock=clif->changelook(&sd->bl, LOOK_WEAPON, sd->status.look.weapon);
#
# --- A5 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: all three are harmless, and an earlier version of the audits doc got
# this wrong twice. A guard of the form `if (x) refreshlook(...)` cannot tell
# an arriving observer that the value is *nothing* — but at enter-view it is
# preceded, unconditionally, by `clif->set_unit_idle`, whose spawn packet
# carries robe, cloth_color and body_style outright. So the observer already
# has the truth, including zero, before the guard runs.
# The rule: this shape can only lose an attribute the spawn packet does NOT
# carry. That was ammunition, and only ammunition. Do not "fix" these.
A5|guarded-resend=LOOK_BODY2 guarded-by if (vd->body_style)
A5|guarded-resend=LOOK_CLOTHES_COLOR guarded-by if (vd->cloth_color)
A5|guarded-resend=LOOK_ROBE guarded-by if (tsd->status.look.robe != 0)
#
# --- A8 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: this is upstream's `status_set_viewdata` memcpy, which zeroes the whole
# view_data when a player is disguised. It stayed a live bug for our fork
# until 2026-07-29 because un-disguise returns through the OTHER branch, which
# assigns fields individually and never re-assigned `ammo`. Now compensated:
# status.c re-derives vd->ammo in the player-class branch beside weapon and
# shield. The memcpy itself is upstream code and stays.
# Any NEW hit here, or any new fork field on view_data, needs the same
# treatment — this audit is the only thing standing between the next one and
# a silent permanent zero.
A8|wholesale-vd-write=memcpy(&sd->vd, vd, sizeof(struct view_data))
#
# --- B2a -----------------------------------------------------------------
# why: no hits. All 14 look types now map to an event (fixed 2026-07-29,
# harness phase 1). The match in version_20220406.rs is EXHAUSTIVE — no `_`
# arm — so the compiler, not this audit, is now the primary tripwire: adding a
# `SpriteChangeType` variant fails to build until somebody decides what it
# means. Verified by temporarily adding a probe variant (E0004).
# A hit reappearing here means a catch-all arm has come back.
#
# --- B2b -----------------------------------------------------------------
# OPEN: B2b — EquipmentEffectPacket is a no-op: that is clif_hat_effect, which
# OPEN:       the server re-sends on enter-view (clif.c:5058). Low priority for
# OPEN:       a classic-era fork, but it is a dropped visual.
# ChangeDirectionPacket and EntityStopMovePacket left this list 2026-07-29 —
# both now produce real events (EntityDirection / EntityStopMove).
# why (all others): correctly ignored. Login/character-server bookkeeping
# (CharacterList, CharacterSlotPage, CharacterBanList, LoginPincode,
# ConnectionRefused), features this fork does not implement (achievements,
# clans, hunting quests, mail, market, reputation, navigation, equip-switch,
# show-equip, personal info, open-ui, map type), and unidentified packets kept
# only for framing (Packet0b18, Packet8302, NotifyActorInit, ChangeMapCell,
# DisplayImage, OpenMarket, UpdateConfiguration, AmmunitionAction).
# A new entry here is a new thing the server says and the client ignores —
# decide deliberately, and record the decision on this line.
B2b|noop=AchievementListPacket
B2b|noop=AchievementUpdatePacket
B2b|noop=AmmunitionActionPacket
B2b|noop=ChangeMapCellPacket
B2b|noop=CharacterBanListPacket
B2b|noop=CharacterListPacket
B2b|noop=CharacterSlotPagePacket
B2b|noop=ClanInfoPacket
B2b|noop=ClanOnlineCountPacket
B2b|noop=ConnectionRefusedPacket
B2b|noop=DisplayImagePacket
B2b|noop=EquipmentEffectPacket
B2b|noop=EquippableSwitchItemListPacket
B2b|noop=HuntingQuestNotificationPacket
B2b|noop=HuntingQuestUpdateObjectivePacket
B2b|noop=HuntingQuestUpdateObjectivePacket4
B2b|noop=LoginPincodePacket
B2b|noop=MapTypePacket
B2b|noop=NavigateToMonsterPacket
B2b|noop=NewMailStatusPacket
B2b|noop=NotifyActorInitPacket
B2b|noop=OpenMarketPacket
B2b|noop=OpenUiPacket
B2b|noop=Packet0b18
B2b|noop=Packet8302
B2b|noop=PersonalInformationPacket
B2b|noop=ReputationPacket
B2b|noop=UpdateConfigurationPacket
B2b|noop=UpdateShowEquipPacket
#
# --- B2c -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The seven appearance fields left this list 2026-07-29: accessory,
# accessory2, accessory3, head_palette, body_palette, robe and body are now
# carried by EntityData and seeded onto `Common`, so they survive spawn,
# respawn, rebuild, enter-view and login without a separate broadcast.
# NOTE they are stored but NOT drawn — sprite composition is still body + head
# + weapon + shield. Rendering them is harness phase 4 and needs accessory
# sprite paths and palette files this tree does not have.
#
# OPEN: B2c — guild identity (guild_id, emblem_version, group_id) and c_level
# OPEN:       are still dropped. Deliberately left out of the phase 1 widening:
# OPEN:       nothing renders a guild emblem or a level tag, and adding unread
# OPEN:       fields would be scope creep. This audit keeps watching them.
# why (the rest): effect_state is kept under the name `option`; `name` arrives
# lazily via UpdateEntityDetails (recovery mechanism 2); object_type is
# consumed at conversion to pick the entity type; honor, virtue, font, x_size,
# y_size and is_boss are unused by this fork.
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=c_level
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=effect_state
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=emblem_version
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=font
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=group_id
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=guild_id
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=honor
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=is_boss
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=name
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=object_type
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=virtue
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=x_size
B2c|spawn-field-dropped=y_size
